<title>SWITZERLAND: CYCLING-TOUR OF SWITZERLAND FIFTH STAGE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TOUR OF SWITZERLAND FIFTH STAGE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SPIEZ, Switzerland 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of</p>
<p>the 31.5km fifth stage time-trial at the Tour of Switzerland on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Sergei Gontchar (Ukraine) 39 minutes, 30 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Jan Ullrich (Germany) same time</p>
<p> 3. Oskar Camenzind (Switzerland)   19 seconds behind</p>
<p> 4. Alex Zuelle (Switzerland)	 30</p>
<p> 5. Yevgeny Berzin (Russia)	   47</p>
<p> 6. Beat Zberg (Switzerland)	  57</p>
<p> 7. Daniele Nardello (Italy)	1:06</p>
<p> 8. Roland Meier (Switzerland)    1:08</p>
<p> 9. Laurent Jalabert (France)     1:24</p>
<p> 10. David Extebarria (Spain)     1:25</p>
<p> 11. Michele Bartoli (Italy)	1:30</p>
<p> 12. Jens Heppner (Germany)	 1:32</p>
<p> 13. Udo Boelts (Germany)	   1:33</p>
<p> 14. Danny Nelissne (Netherlands) 1:46</p>
<p> 15. Gianni Faresin (Italy)	 1:47</p>
<p>Leading overall placings after the fifth stage:</p>
<p> 1. Christophe Agnolutto (France) 14 hours, 44 minutes, 26</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p> 2. Valentino Fois (Italy)	 4:01 behind</p>
<p> 3. Ullrich			    6:23</p>
<p> 4. Camenzind			  7:27</p>
<p> 5. Meier				8:07</p>
<p> 6. Zuelle			     8:30</p>
<p> 7. Zberg				8:46</p>
<p> 8. Boelts			     8:55</p>
<p> 9. Danny Nelissen (Netherlands) 9:01</p>
<p> 10. Heppner			   9:19</p>
